Rem ==================================================================
Rem seed-math.shoddy — reckoner seed: math.shoddy's derived layer
Rem
Rem Bridges the geometry, interpolation and logarithm words math.shoddy
Rem adds on top of the engine core's own trig and logs. RckSeedMath(st)
Rem is the whole of this file's public surface: fold it over a state and
Rem LOGB, LOG2, HYPOT, DIST, CLAMP, LERP, REMAP and ROUNDTO are in the
Rem dictionary.
Rem
Rem NOT BRIDGED: Rad and Deg. The engine already owns DEG/RAD as the
Rem angle mode (R4.7), and a program that wants degree/radian conversion
Rem as a VALUE rather than a mode still has DEG SIN and RAD SIN to hand —
Rem bridging math's Rad/Deg here would give two spellings for one idea
Rem and the wrong one would be the one that gets used by habit.
Rem
Rem Every word here pre-flights the division or logarithm math.shoddy's
Rem plain "/" and Log would otherwise abort on — R4.1 applied to a
Rem machine that was written before the no-abort contract existed, and so
Rem carries none of its own guards.
Rem ==================================================================

Include "math.shoddy"
Include "cuttle.shoddy"
Include "reckoner.shoddy"
Include "seq.shoddy"

Rem ---- pulling several numeric arguments at once -----------------------
Rem The reckoner's own RckNumArg reads one; a word of arity 3 or more
Rem reads several, deepest first, and stops at the first one that is not
Rem a NUMBER.

Def MNums(word As String, vs As List Of Cell) As Result
    MNumsAt(word, vs, 1, { })

Def MNumsAt(word As String, vs As List Of Cell, k As Number, acc As List Of Number) As Result
    If k > Length(vs) Then
        Ok(acc)
    Else
        MNumsNext(word, vs, k, acc, RckNumArg(word, Nth(vs, k)))

Def MNumsNext(word As String, vs As List Of Cell, k As Number, acc As List Of Number, r As Result) As Result
    Select Case r
        Case Ok(x)
            MNumsAt(word, vs, k + 1, Append(acc, x))
        Case Err(w, at)
            Err(w, at)
        Case Else
            Err(word & " did not answer", 0)

Rem ---- LOGB, LOG2 --------------------------------------------------------
Rem Both refuse before Log is asked to: a non-positive x or a base of 1
Rem would otherwise carry a plain "/" straight into abort.

Def MSeedLogb(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "LOGB", 2, RckPure(Fn(vs) => MLogb(vs)), "( base x -- log )", "Logarithm of x to the given base.")

Def MLogb(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case MNums("LOGB", vs)
        Case Ok(ns)
            MLogbAt(Nth(ns, 1), Nth(ns, 2))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("LOGB did not answer")

Def MLogbAt(base As Number, x As Number) As RckWork
    If x <= 0 Then
        RckWorkBad("LOGB has no answer for x at or below zero")
    Else
        If base <= 0 Or base = 1 Then
            RckWorkBad("LOGB needs a base greater than zero and not equal to one")
        Else
            RckVals({ CutNum(LogBase(base, x)) })

Def MSeedLog2(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "LOG2", 1, RckPure(Fn(vs) => RckLift1("LOG2", vs, >(0), "has no answer at or below zero", Log2)), "( x -- log2 x )", "Logarithm base two; refuses zero and below.")

Rem ---- HYPOT, DIST --------------------------------------------------------
Rem Both total: a sum of squares under a square root never goes negative.

Def MSeedHypot(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "HYPOT", 2, RckPure(Fn(vs) => RckLift2("HYPOT", vs, RckAlways2, "", Hypot)), "( x y -- h )", "The length of the hypotenuse of a right triangle with legs x and y.")

Def MSeedDist(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "DIST", 4, RckPure(Fn(vs) => MDist(vs)), "( x0 y0 x1 y1 -- d )", "The distance between two points.")

Def MDist(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case MNums("DIST", vs)
        Case Ok(ns)
            RckVals({ CutNum(Dist(Nth(ns, 1), Nth(ns, 2), Nth(ns, 3), Nth(ns, 4))) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("DIST did not answer")

Rem ---- CLAMP, LERP, REMAP -------------------------------------------------
Rem CLAMP and LERP are total for any lo/hi or a/b, even out of order.
Rem REMAP divides by the input span, so an input range of zero width is
Rem refused before Remap's own InvLerp is asked to divide by it.

Def MSeedClamp(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "CLAMP", 3, RckPure(Fn(vs) => MClamp(vs)), "( x lo hi -- y )", "x held between lo and hi.")

Def MClamp(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case MNums("CLAMP", vs)
        Case Ok(ns)
            RckVals({ CutNum(Clamp(Nth(ns, 1), Nth(ns, 2), Nth(ns, 3))) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("CLAMP did not answer")

Def MSeedLerp(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "LERP", 3, RckPure(Fn(vs) => MLerp(vs)), "( a b t -- y )", "Linear interpolation between a and b at fraction t.")

Def MLerp(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case MNums("LERP", vs)
        Case Ok(ns)
            RckVals({ CutNum(Lerp(Nth(ns, 1), Nth(ns, 2), Nth(ns, 3))) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("LERP did not answer")

Def MSeedRemap(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "REMAP", 5, RckPure(Fn(vs) => MRemap(vs)), "( x inLo inHi outLo outHi -- y )", "Map x from one range onto another, linearly.")

Def MRemap(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case MNums("REMAP", vs)
        Case Ok(ns)
            MRemapAt(ns)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("REMAP did not answer")

Def MRemapAt(ns As List Of Number) As RckWork
    If Nth(ns, 2) = Nth(ns, 3) Then
        RckWorkBad("REMAP needs an input range with two different ends")
    Else
        RckVals({ CutNum(Remap(Nth(ns, 1), Nth(ns, 2), Nth(ns, 3), Nth(ns, 4), Nth(ns, 5))) })

Rem ---- ROUNDTO ------------------------------------------------------------
Rem RoundTo raises 10 to the power of n; the same magnitude bound the
Rem engine core's own ^ enforces keeps that finite.

Def MSeedRoundto(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "ROUNDTO", 2, RckPure(Fn(vs) => RckLift2("ROUNDTO", vs, MRoundOk, "needs a place count no wider than 15", RoundTo)), "( x n -- y )", "x rounded to n decimal places.")

Def MRoundOk(x As Number, n As Number) As Boolean
    Abs(n) <= 15

Rem ---- the seed -----------------------------------------------------------

Def RckSeedMath(st As RckState) As RckState
    Let st1 = MSeedLogb(RckSeeding(st, "seed-math"))
    Let st2 = MSeedLog2(st1)
    Let st3 = MSeedHypot(st2)
    Let st4 = MSeedDist(st3)
    Let st5 = MSeedClamp(st4)
    Let st6 = MSeedLerp(st5)
    Let st7 = MSeedRemap(st6)
    MSeedRoundto(st7)
